25
00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:47.000
It's necessary and sufficient for producing helplessness. Now very interesting, it turns out there is a circuit from up here in the forebrain, the medial frontal lobes. There's a specific circuit that goes down to the dorsal refrain nucleus. and turns it off. And it turns it off when you learn mastery, when you have hope. So it turns out that contrary to what we thought 50 years ago, and this is one of the great things about being in a science for 50 years,
它是产生无助感的必要且充分条件。现在非常有趣的是，事实证明，从这里的前脑，即内侧额叶，有一条回路。有一条特定的回路通向背侧中缝核，并将其关闭。当你学会掌控、当你拥有希望时，它就会关闭它。所以事实证明，与我们50年前的想法相反——这也是从事科学研究50年的伟大之处之一，

26
00:18:47.000 --> 00:19:23.000
you can find out you're wrong. We found out we were wrong. Being helpless is the default mammalian reaction to troubles. were born helpless. The default reaction is to give up. What we have, however, what humans have is a circuit, which I call the hope circuit, which when it's ignited by mastery and hope turns off helplessness. So it turns out what's learned in helplessness experiments is hope and mastery,
你可以发现自己错了。我们发现我们错了。无助是哺乳动物面对麻烦时的默认反应。我们生来就是无助的。默认反应是放弃。然而，我们所拥有的，人类所拥有的，是一条回路，我称之为“希望回路”，当它被掌控感和希望点燃时，就会关闭无助感。所以事实证明，在无助实验中习得的是希望和掌控感，

