00:24:32.000 --> 00:25:16.000
noticed that since my fifth birthday, I haven't whined once? I said, oh, yeah. Yeah, Nikki, that's right. He says, well, Daddy, on my fifth birthday, I decided that I wasn't going to whine anymore. And that was the hardest thing I've ever done. And if I can stop whining, you can stop being such a grouch. And she hit the nail on the head. In three different ways, all of a sudden, I realized three different things. First, that she was right and that I was a grouch. And indeed, what I thought, what I was so proud about was my ability to see what was wrong with everything.
“自从我五岁生日以来，我一次都没抱怨过？”我说：“哦，是的。是的，尼基，没错。”她说：“嗯，爸爸，在我五岁生日那天，我决定我再也不抱怨了。那是我做过的最难的事情。如果我能停止抱怨，你也能停止做一个脾气暴躁的人。”她一针见血。突然之间，我意识到了三件事。首先，她是对的，我确实是个脾气暴躁的人。事实上，我引以为豪的是我能看出每件事有什么问题。

35
00:25:16.000 --> 00:26:01.000
And I realized for the first time, maybe any success I had in life was not because of being a pessimist and a grouch and a critic, but maybe it was because I could sometimes see what was right rather than what was wrong. And I decided to change. And indeed, I have. I measure these things not only in the general population, but in myself. So the first thing was, Nikki was right, and I was a grouch, and maybe being a grouch really got in the way of doing what I wanted in life. And the second thing I realized was that my theory of child rearing was wrong. So my theory of child rearing in education was remedial.
我第一次意识到，也许我在生活中取得的任何成功，并不是因为我是一个悲观主义者、一个脾气暴躁的人和一个批评家，而是因为我有时能看到什么是对的，而不是什么是错的。我决定改变。事实上，我确实改变了。我不仅在普通人群中衡量这些东西，也在我自己身上衡量。所以第一件事是，尼基是对的，我确实是个脾气暴躁的人，也许这种脾气真的阻碍了我做我想做的事。第二件事我意识到的是，我的育儿理论是错误的。所以我的育儿和教育理论是补救性的。

