00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:56.000
It basically said that what our job as teachers and parents to do was to find out what our kids were doing wrong and correct them. And somehow if we corrected all of their errors, we get an exemplary child. Well, it struck me that that's nonsense. What you get then is a child that's not doing anything wrong. But your job as a parent and a teacher is to find out what the kid does right. what they're strong at. And what I saw on Nikki now was her ability to talk sense to adults and to identify that strength and to get your child or your or your student to live their life around what they do well, not to spend their life avoiding what they do badly. So that was the second
它基本上说，我们作为老师和父母的工作是找出孩子们做错了什么并纠正他们。如果纠正了他们所有的错误，我们就能得到一个模范孩子。嗯，这让我觉得那是胡扯。你得到的是一个什么错都不犯的孩子。但你作为父母和老师的工作是找出孩子做对了什么，他们擅长什么。我现在在尼基身上看到的是她与成年人讲道理的能力，识别那种优势，并让你的孩子或学生围绕他们擅长的事情生活，而不是花一生去避免他们做得不好的事情。所以那是第二

